Heavy Periods and Period Cramps: How to Make Difficult Days More Manageable

Heavy periods can sometimes occur alongside menstrual cramps, making certain days of your cycle particularly uncomfortable.

While menstrual flow and cramps are different experiences, dealing with both at the same time can make everyday activities more difficult.

Why Can Period Days Feel So Uncomfortable?

During menstruation, the uterus contracts to help shed its lining. These contractions can cause cramps for some people.

At the same time, heavier menstrual flow may require more frequent pad changes and greater attention to leakage protection.

Choose Comfortable Period Protection

When your period is heavy, your sanitary pad should provide appropriate absorbency and coverage while remaining comfortable against your skin.

